+\section{Hardware and Software Requirements}
+This project is a research pipeline, so the requirements below cover developing and running the experiments in Chapter 5. They do not cover deploying a user-facing application.
+
+\subsection{Hardware Requirements}
+\begin{itemize}
+    \item \textbf{GPUs.} Running RNAPro inference, and training or fine-tuning it if full retraining is carried out, requires high-memory GPUs. The original RNAPro work used eight GB300 GPUs because of the model's large memory requirements. This project will use the closest to this that is available.
+    \item \textbf{CPU and memory.} Sufficient CPU cores and system memory to run the template search methods, build features, and compute TM-align labels for all candidate templates in the training and validation splits.
+    \item \textbf{Storage.} Sufficient disk space for the PDB structures with C1$'$ coordinates, the MSAs, the Eigen dataset, the candidate templates and their stored labels, and the model checkpoints.
+\end{itemize}
+
+\subsection{Software Requirements}
+\begin{itemize}
+    \item \textbf{Prediction model.} RNAPro (Lee et al., 2025), which is built on the Protenix AlphaFold~3 reproduction, together with the Protenix base checkpoints used for initialization.
+    \item \textbf{Template search tools.} MMseqs2, Infernal with Rfam, and tools for embedding-based and secondary-structure-aware search. BEAGLE is a candidate tool for secondary-structure-aware search and is not yet confirmed.
+    \item \textbf{MSA generation.} The rMSA pipeline, with T converted to U in its outputs.
+    \item \textbf{Structure scoring.} US-align, run with the C$1'$ atom and sequence-independent alignment, for TM-align labels, model evaluation, and near-duplicate template comparison.
+    \item \textbf{RNA language models.} RNet2 (default) and AIDO.RNA, plus other models chosen later for the language-model comparison.
+    \item \textbf{Data.} PDB structures, the Eigen dataset of up-to-date sequences and MSAs, and a structural-similarity benchmark for template-poor targets (RNA3DB is planned).
+    \item \textbf{Selector model.} A ranking or regression model, whose type is not yet fixed, together with the software needed to train and tune it.
+\end{itemize}
+
